title: MikroTik IP Pools
agents: mikrotik
catalog: hw/network/mikrotik
license: GPL
distribution: check_mk
description:
 Usage of the IP pools of a MikroTik RouterOS 7 device ({/ip/pool}) as
 used by the DHCP server, PPP or hotspot. The agent counts the used
 addresses from {/ip/pool/used}; the leases themselves are not
 transferred.

 The pool size is computed from the ranges (from-to, prefix or single
 address, several separated by commas). Used addresses in percent have
 upper levels (default {WARN} at 80%, {CRIT} at 90%), free addresses
 optionally lower levels. A configured next pool is shown. Levels via
 the rule {MikroTik IP Pools}.

 To connect to the MikroTik device a special datasource program is
 used: {MikroTik RouterOS} in Setup > Agents > Other integrations,
 module "IP pools". The module is opt-in, "all" does not include it.

item:
 The name of the pool.

perfdata:
 Used addresses in percent, used and free addresses.

inventory:
 One service per pool.
